model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.accountPresentation {
    metadata {
      constraint "An app's Accounts tab shows one section per service in each scope. Requirements join one section when their providers' names are equal or one opens with the other and a space (\"Service\" and \"Service MCP\"), every one takes many accounts, and no two share a provider; requirements that share a provider are roles and keep their own sections, as do requirements of different scopes or contribution policies and host-provisioned, retained, native-API and provider-app-only requirements. Each account stays linked to its own requirement, so tool resolution and saved links are unchanged and an account is listed once. The section's one Connect new account offers every open method by its existing label, opening the connect dialog at that method's requirement; a label repeated by a requirement of the same name is offered once, and labels repeated across names add the requirement's name. Where the joined names differ, each row names the part it serves, and rows say which declared catalog tool sections their requirement and method can't run. Provider declarations are never changed to merge sections, since they are saved accounts' identity. The naming prompt after a connection prefills the title the account gets anyway, and the identity a sign-in's check reports replaces it until someone types; the untouched prefilled title waits for that check before saving, while a name someone authored never waits, and keeping the default preserves the generated label."
    }
  }
}
